From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 15:15:52 +0100
Subject: net: dsa: mxl862xx: increase old firmware CMD timeout

Lift the command timeout by 10x from 500ms to 5s.
This is done because older firmware can be extremely slow to respond
and cause -ETIMEOUT during setup, or crash the PHY state machine.

The BPI-R4 Pro 8X Phase 9 runtime showed MxL86252C firmware 1.0.70 and
DSA setup timeouts while configuring the 802.1Q tag path, so keep this
as an OpenWrt downstream old-firmware compatibility patch rather than a
firmware update requirement.

Source: OpenWrt PR #21083 pending patch
  refs/upstream/openwrt-main-pr21083/target/linux/generic/pending-6.12/
  760-27-DO-NOT-SUBMIT-net-dsa-mxl862xx-increase-CMD-timeout.patch
Behavior source: BPI-R4 Pro 8X Phase 9 runtime evidence with MxL86252C
firmware 1.0.70 and -ETIMEDOUT during DSA setup.
Adapted-for: ImmortalWrt 25.12 / Linux 6.12.91 BPI-R4 Pro 8X Phase 9
Adapted-by: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5)

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-host.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-host.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-host.c
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@ static int mxl862xx_busy_wait(struct mxl
 	int val;
 
 	return readx_poll_timeout(mxl862xx_ctrl_read, priv, val,
-				  !(val & CTRL_BUSY_MASK), 15, 500000);
+				  !(val & CTRL_BUSY_MASK), 50, 5000000);
 }
 
 /* Issue a firmware command with CRC-6 protection on the ctrl and len_ret
